                "tuning.feel.step1.title": "1. Listen to the Motor Pitch",
                "tuning.feel.step1.body": "A healthy rotary produces a smooth, consistent electric hum. If the pitch sags, sputters, or drops when the needle enters skin, the motor is struggling against membrane tension or tissue drag. If it screams at a high whine, the motor is over-revving.",
                "tuning.feel.step2.title": "2. Inspect the Needle Entry",
                "tuning.feel.step2.body": "Lines should deposit pigment crisply on a single continuous pass. If the needle snags or skips, do not just push harder: evaluate whether needle stroke or voltage needs a 0.2V-0.4V increase. For shading, look for controlled stipple dots rather than gouging tears.",
                "tuning.feel.step3.title": "3. Adjust in Minimal Increments",
